      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consider the air flowing over the curved surface of the wing. As it speeds up, the molecules of the air exert a counterclockwise force on the wing. However, Newton's third law also states that the air exerts an equal and opposite force on the wing. This means the air molecules push outward on the wing, also counterclockwise. The combination of these two opposing forces creates the upward lift, as the overall effect is an upward force exerted on the wing by the air.",
      "source": "target",
