    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, I think I'm getting confused. If the air is pushing \"outward\" or counterclockwise, wouldn't that just push the wing sideways? I thought Newton's law in this context was about the air being deflected downwards by the wing. Can you explain the \"downwash\" part and how that relates to the reaction force pushing the wing up?",
